site: the footer lists no pages; the header menu is the whole menu

The footer's "More" block restated the menu for pages the menu had already declined to carry.
What is left is what a footer is for: who we are, where, how to reach us, then Follow and the
legal line.

- `_includes/footer.html`: the page list goes.
- `_data/nav.yml`: `footer` becomes `elsewhere`, which renders nowhere. The `page` layout prints
  no `<h1>`, so it is the only way the header can still name the page you are on.

Consequence, written down rather than hidden: `/about/`, `/nonprofits/` and
`/policies/non-discrimination/` are now linked from nothing and still sit in `/sitemap.xml`.
That is the honest state of a page nobody has decided to carry. `/contact/` and `/check-in/` are
still reached from inside pages.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] `bundle exec jekyll build` clean
- [x] Playwright `--grep-invert @external`: 553 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed
- [x] the header still names `/about/` and the other `elsewhere` pages
